WEBVTT

00:00:00.109 --> 00:00:10.717
This video shows how a teacher marks daily attendance on a phone. You will open Manual Entry, mark everyone present, change the exceptions, and save.

00:00:12.397 --> 00:00:19.453
Tap the menu button at the top left, open Attendance, and then tap 1. Manual Entry.

00:00:19.909 --> 00:00:30.085
The class is already chosen, here Class 1 - A. Tap the date field and choose the day you are marking. The students of that class appear in a list below.

00:00:31.402 --> 00:00:42.634
Tap Mark All Present. Every student now shows a green P, and the count at the top says 4 Present. A short key above the list explains the letters.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:57.428
Now change only the exceptions. Each tap on a student's letter turns P for present into A for absent, and one more tap makes it L for leave. Here one student is now absent and another is on leave.

00:00:58.382 --> 00:01:05.390
The counts at the top update as you go. Here they show 2 Present, 1 Absent and 1 Leave.

00:01:06.302 --> 00:01:13.886
Scroll down and tap Save Attendance. A green message says Saved, 4 created, 0 updated.

00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:22.298
Attendance is saved. Repeat these steps for each class and each day.
